---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { holdE1A6Stats } from '../../data/claims';
import { url } from '../../data/site';

const s = holdE1A6Stats;
const n = (v: number) => v.toLocaleString('en-GB');
---
<Base
  locale="en"
  slug="hold"
  title="HOLD — Experiment E1-A6"
  description="Results of the E1-A6 experiment: 99 runs, three conditions, hypotheses H1/H2/H3, independent audit by Harv Banning."
  kicker="Experiment"
  lede="The same model, left alone, executed 66 violations. Under HOLD, none — and 8 missions completed with a receipt. 99 runs, three conditions, one independent audit, and what none of it shows."
  sources="HOLD · skiredj-prog/hold repository · commit f3bb683 · Harv Banning audit archive of 3 November 2026"
>

  <div class="hold-stats">
    <div><strong class="is-stop">{s.conditions.A.violations}</strong><span>violations executed — A, agent alone</span></div>
    <div><strong class="is-warn">{s.conditions.B.violations}</strong><span>violations — B, cautious agent + human</span></div>
    <div><strong class="is-ok">{s.conditions.C.violations}</strong><span>violations — C, under HOLD</span></div>
    <div><strong class="is-ok">{s.conditions.C.completed}/{s.conditions.C.runs}</strong><span>missions completed with a receipt — C</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Distribution of the 99 runs</h2>

  <p>Each dot is one run. Three conditions, 33 runs each, across 11 scenarios. Only condition C carries HOLD: A is the same model left to itself, B a cautious agent assisted by a simulated human.</p>

  <div class="hold-chart">
    <div class="hold-row">
      <span class="hold-row-label">A</span>
      <div class="hold-dots">
        {Array.from({ length: s.conditions.A.runsWithExecutedBooking }, (_, i) => (
          <span class="hold-dot is-violation" title={`A-${i + 1} · booking executed on invented values`}></span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hold-row">
      <span class="hold-row-label">B</span>
      <div class="hold-dots">
        {Array.from({ length: s.conditions.B.violations }, (_, i) => (
          <span class="hold-dot is-violation" title={`B-${i + 1} · violation`}></span>
        ))}
        {Array.from({ length: s.conditions.B.runs - s.conditions.B.violations }, (_, i) => (
          <span class="hold-dot is-other" title={`B-${i + 4} · other outcome`}></span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hold-row">
      <span class="hold-row-label">C</span>
      <div class="hold-dots">
        {Array.from({ length: s.conditions.C.completed }, (_, i) => (
          <span class="hold-dot is-completed" title={`C-${i + 1} · CLOSED_COMPLETED`}></span>
        ))}
        {Array.from({ length: s.conditions.C.unconfirmed }, (_, i) => (
          <span class="hold-dot is-unconfirmed" title={`C-${i + 9} · CLOSED_UNCONFIRMED`}></span>
        ))}
        {Array.from({ length: s.conditions.C.noEffect }, (_, i) => (
          <span class="hold-dot is-noeffect" title={`C-${i + 31} · CLOSED_NO_EFFECT`}></span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="hold-legend">
      <li><span class="hold-dot is-violation"></span>Run with an executed violation</li>
      <li><span class="hold-dot is-completed"></span>CLOSED_COMPLETED</li>
      <li><span class="hold-dot is-unconfirmed"></span>CLOSED_UNCONFIRMED</li>
      <li><span class="hold-dot is-noeffect"></span>CLOSED_NO_EFFECT</li>
      <li><span class="hold-dot is-other"></span>Other outcome</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="hold-source-line">A counts 33 runs with an executed booking, for 66 violation categories (values never observed + price not verifiable). Source: <code>E1_A6_RESULTS.md</code>, the “What happened” table · commit <code>f3bb683</code></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Hypotheses</h2>

  <div class="hold-hyp">
    <article class="is-accepted">
      <p class="hold-verdict">Accepted — E1-A6 scope</p>
      <h3>H1 — Execution integrity</h3>
      <p>Zero violations executed across the 33 runs under HOLD, with a floor genuinely exercised: 164 effect proposals reached it. Counterfactual on the same model, tools and messages: left alone, that model booked on invented values in 33 runs out of 33.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="is-accepted">
      <p class="hold-verdict">Accepted</p>
      <h3>H2 — Legitimate progress</h3>
      <p>Condition C: 8 CLOSED_COMPLETED, 22 CLOSED_UNCONFIRMED, 3 CLOSED_NO_EFFECT, 0 violations. Condition B: 0 legitimate completions for 3 violations. Legitimate completions proceed without artificial blocking.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="is-open">
      <p class="hold-verdict">Not evaluated</p>
      <h3>H3 — Contextual discernment</h3>
      <p>Outside the scope of E1-A6. The hypothesis stays open, for a separate experiment to address.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Independent audit — Harv Banning, 3 November 2026</h2>

  <p>{n(s.audit.totalChecks)} checks were re-run against the 99 traces: {n(s.audit.passed)} passed, {s.audit.failed} diverged. All {s.audit.failed} divergences fall in the <code>source_fingerprint_raw</code> category — a CRLF line-ending artefact with no semantic bearing.</p>

  <p>{n(s.audit.eventHashesRecomputed)} event hashes were recomputed and {s.audit.mutationControlsDetected} mutation controls detected.</p>

  <blockquote class="hold-quote">
    <p>Verdict returned: <strong>qualified support, not certification</strong>.</p>
    <p class="hold-quote-note">The auditor adds that unqualified frozen-protocol acceptance is not established: 22 of 23 raw fingerprints fail (all resolve under CRLF→LF normalisation), H1’s full stated condition scope is absent from the delivered source, and B’s completion wording is ambiguous. AI-assisted audit, with no human reviewer signature.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Explicit limits</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>The results belong to E1-A6 (Llama 3.2 3B, synthetic hotel environment). They do not generalise without a new experiment.</li>
    <li>The experiment does not isolate which component of the HOLD condition produces the effect: H2 compares the whole — floor, reconciliation, agent contract — against condition B, not the floor alone.</li>
    <li>Exploratory status: the A6 protocol was designed after reading the A5 traces, on the same scenarios and seeds.</li>
    <li>Governor isolation is not complete in the B1 batch. The bypass is documented on an experimental branch, not merged into production.</li>
    <li>The audit is AI-assisted and carries no human reviewer signature.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sources and anchors</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/skiredj-prog/hold/tree/f3bb683" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HOLD repository, commit <code>f3bb683</code> ↗</a></li>
    <li><code>docs/audit/harv-banning-2026-11-03/</code> — full audit archive</li>
  </ul>

  <p><a href={url('/en/claims/')}>Full claims register →</a><br /><a href={url('/en/credibility/')}>TENIR-Gov credibility journey →</a></p>

</Base>

<style>
  .hold-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(8.5rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0 0 2.2rem;
  }
  .hold-stats > div { background: var(--bg-raised); padding: 1.1rem; min-width: 0; }
  .hold-stats strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .hold-stats strong.is-stop { color: #c0564d; }
  .hold-stats strong.is-warn { color: #9a6b1e; }
  .hold-stats strong.is-ok { color: var(--ok); }
  .hold-stats span { display: block; font-size: .76rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .45rem; line-height: 1.4; }

  .hold-chart {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.4rem;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    margin: 1.2rem 0 2.4rem;
  }
  .hold-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .85rem; margin-bottom: .7rem; }
  .hold-row-label {
    font: 600 .78rem var(--mono);
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 1.1rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .hold-dots { display: flex; gap: .32rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .hold-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: .8rem;
    height: .8rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .hold-dot.is-violation { background: #c0564d; }
  .hold-dot.is-completed { background: #2d7a63; }
  .hold-dot.is-unconfirmed { background: #7d93a2; }
  .hold-dot.is-noeffect { background: #c08a35; }
  .hold-dot.is-other { background: var(--line); border: 1px solid var(--muted); }

  .hold-legend {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: .5rem 1.1rem;
    font-size: .76rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .hold-legend li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; margin: 0; }
  .hold-legend .hold-dot { width: .65rem; height: .65rem; }
  .hold-source-line { font-size: .74rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; }

  .hold-hyp {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: .9rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 2.4rem;
  }
  .hold-hyp article {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.15rem;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
  }
  .hold-hyp article.is-accepted { border-left-color: #2d7a63; }
  .hold-hyp article.is-open { border-left-color: var(--muted); }
  .hold-verdict {
    font: 600 .68rem var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: .05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 .45rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .hold-hyp article.is-accepted .hold-verdict { color: #2d7a63; }
  .hold-hyp h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .hold-hyp p { font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .hold-quote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: .2rem 0 .2rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .hold-quote p { margin: 0 0 .4rem; }
  .hold-quote-note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-stats strong.is-stop { color: #e39a93; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-stats strong.is-warn { color: #dfb871; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-dot.is-violation { background: #d9766c; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-dot.is-completed { background: #5aba9b; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-dot.is-unconfirmed { background: #8ba3b2; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-dot.is-noeffect { background: #dcaa5e; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-hyp article.is-accepted { border-left-color: #5aba9b; }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .hold-hyp article.is-accepted .hold-verdict { color: #5aba9b; }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .hold-stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .hold-hyp { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
